### What did I learn this week?

This week in I&S, we had a debate about strong dictatorships compared to weak democracies. I learned how to defend my opinion and use examples to support my argument.

### What was my biggest achievement?

I think my biggest achievement was making a really good rebuttal. I challenged the other team to name six benevolent dictators, but they could only name one. I replied, "I said six, not one."

They then challenged me to name six good leaders from weak democracies. I said, "Yes, I can, unlike you," and I managed to name six. I felt proud because I was able to think quickly and respond confidently.

### What was challenging?

The challenging part was thinking of strong arguments and responding quickly when the other team challenged me.

### What do I want to improve?

I want to become better at debating by using stronger evidence and explaining why my examples support my argument, instead of just naming them.
